EnderGram 1.0.0
Project: https://github.com/SujayPro/EnderDesk
Telegram channel: https://t.me/EnderGramNews
Chat: https://t.me/EnderGramChat
===================================

EnderGram is an independent fork of the AyuGram Desktop codebase, which is
itself a fork of Telegram Desktop.

Upstream application: https://github.com/AyuGram/AyuGramDesktop
Telegram Desktop:     https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop
Linux packaging base: https://github.com/stillemptyNOW/AyuGram-For-Linux

The Telegram-compatible engine is the upstream GPL-3.0 (with OpenSSL
exception) application. The EnderGram launcher and branding build tooling
are released under GPL-3.0-or-later.

This is an unofficial community build. It is not affiliated with Telegram FZ-LLC,
AyuGram, or Radolyn Labs. AyuGram includes features that may violate
Telegram's Terms of Service. Use at your own risk.

The complete corresponding source is available in the EnderGram project
directory supplied with this build, including the upstream source tree.


Design note
-----------
The dark palette is inspired by the public design language of Command Code
(commandcode.ai). No Command Code artwork, logo, copy, code, or private
Figma files are included. The theme is a palette-only interpretation.


Window decoration note
----------------------
The default launch writes a scoped KWin rule to the user's
~/.config/kwinrulesrc (backup: kwinrulesrc.endergram.bak) to remove the native
titlebar from EnderGram's main window. Use --titlebar to opt out.
